  "details": "Before one of the updates certain avatars had a Physbone type that could have their position locked by pressing the top trigger on the controller while grabbing them like for example stretching an ear then locking it so it’s insanely long no longer works \n\nHow to recreate \n\nSwitch to an avatar that has Physbones\n\nGrab and pull or move the Physbone to a different place \n\nTry to lock its position and watch as it just goes back to its default position\n\nI’m playing on quest 2 this does not effect pc Physbones work fine on there\n\nAnother thing I have noticed Physbones are separate on pc and quest if someone is messing with the physbones on your avatar while you’re on pc and they are on quest you can no longer see them moving the physbones this might have something to do with why physbones can’t have their positions locked on quest",
